      "descripcion": "A gale-force, non-tropical low pressure area located a few hundred miles south of Bermuda is producing an area of cloudiness and showers. This system could acquire some subtropical characteristics during the next couple of days while it moves slowly eastward over the western and central subtropical Atlantic. By late this weekend, upper-level winds are forecast to become unfavorable for further development. While a new non-tropical low could form from the remnants of the current low early next week, environmental conditions are unlikely to support significant development. Regardless, gale-force winds are likely over parts of the central subtropical Atlantic through the weekend. For more information, including Gale Warnings, please see High Seas Forecasts issued by the National Weather Service.",
